From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OHOS PC Developer <ohpcd@example.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Jul 2026 10:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: bypass pkg-config for curses on OHOS

OHOS CI workers ship the ncurses static library (libncursesw.a) and
headers under /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/{include,lib} but
do NOT install a curses.pc / ncurses.pc pkg-config file. As a result
meson's dependency('curses') fails at the pkg-config stage with:

  Run-time dependency curses found: NO
  (tried pkg-config, pkg-config, pkg-config, pkg-config,
   config-tool and system)

Replace dependency('curses') with cc.find_library('ncursesw') plus an
explicit include_directories() pointing at the OHOS system include
path. This mirrors the approach used by the hexcurse and fdclone
recipes (autotools, -I/-L injection) but adapted for meson's
find_library API.

No source code logic changes — only the dependency discovery method.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OHOS-specific path]
Signed-off-by: OHOS PC Developer <ohpcd@example.com>

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -142,7 +142,15 @@ if is_windows
         link_args: ['-L' + deps_lib_path, '-lpdcurses']
     )
 else
-    curses = dependency('curses', required : true)
+    # OHOS: system provides libncursesw.a + headers at /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local
+    # but no curses.pc pkg-config file. Use cc.find_library() to bypass pkg-config.
+    ncurses_lib = cc.find_library('ncursesw',
+        dirs: ['/storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/lib'],
+        required: true)
+    curses = declare_dependency(
+        dependencies: [ncurses_lib],
+        include_directories: include_directories('/storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/include')
+    )
 endif

 # Define some curses preprocessor symbols
